A custom format test asks whether one release matches one format. A quality profile test asks a different question: when every custom format in a profile scores the same set of releases, do they come out in the order you want?

That question has no pass or fail. You don't tell Profilarr what score a release should get. Instead you save the releases you care about, pick a profile, and read the scores. When you change a custom format or a score, you come back to the same releases and check the order still makes sense.

<Callout type="info">

Think of a quality profile test as a search simulation. Instead of editing, syncing, and running an interactive search for every score change, you run the search once and keep its releases. Profilarr scores them against your latest changes straight away.

</Callout>

## Adding Movies and Series

Rather than storing tests under each quality profile, Profilarr stores them under the movies and series whose releases you're testing. Every profile in the database can score the same releases, so you can switch between profiles and see how each one ranks the same search.



Open **Testing** under **Quality Profiles**. Each linked database has its own tab. Press **Add Entity** (`+`), search TMDB for a movie or series, and select as many results as you like. Each one becomes a row you can add releases to.

<ThemeImage
	dark="/images/docs_qp_testing_add[style=dark].png"
	light="/images/docs_qp_testing_add[style=light].png"
	alt="Profilarr's Add Test Entity dialog over the Testing page, with a TMDB search for Blade Runner. Blade Runner 2049 (2017) and Blade Runner (1982) are checked as movies, Blade Runner: Black Lotus (2021) is an unchecked TV series, and both movies are listed under Selected (2) above the Add button."
	caption="Adding Blade Runner and Blade Runner 2049 from a TMDB search."
	border />

<Callout type="info">

Profilarr looks movies and series up on TMDB, so it needs a [TMDB token](https://www.themoviedb.org/settings/api) before you can add any. Open **Settings > General**, and paste your **API Read Access Token** (not the API key) from your TMDB account into **TMDB Configuration**. Press **Test** to check it works.

</Callout>

## Adding Releases

Each movie or series has two ways to add releases.

